---
/**
 * /profile: the person's own profile, and the Profile Record editor, on one
 * page. MASTER-SPEC 3.1 (Person) for the identity header, 3.2 (Profile
 * Record) for the record beneath it, F2 for the record-building outcome
 * ("a person can build their record in under 20 minutes: entries,
 * artifacts, classifications") and its import boost. The owner's words,
 * verbatim: "like LinkedIn, the user should have a profile page and should
 * be able to edit that profile page on the page."
 *
 * MERGED FROM TWO PAGES INTO ONE. This used to be src/pages/account/profile.astro
 * (the identity header plus a read-only render of the record) and
 * src/pages/account/record.astro (the structured editor: add an entry, the
 * resume-import boost, every entry's edit/delete/artifact forms) at two
 * separate addresses, both rendering the same record through the same
 * RecordView, both posting to the same three endpoints. Two pages for one
 * resource meant two places the "where does a save send you back to" bug
 * below could recur, and two URLs a signed-in reader had to already know
 * apart. One page, one URL, ends that: /account/record no longer exists,
 * and everything it did lives here.
 *
 * IT READS AS A RECORD, NOT A FORM. The rule this page is now built on:
 * nothing renders an empty form until it is summoned. Before this rebuild the
 * page rendered, on load, an upload form, a paste form, an add-entry form, an
 * add-link form, and one empty add-artifact form under every single entry. The
 * import band is a state machine with one action at a time; the record is one
 * row per entry with everything else behind its own disclosure; the add-entry
 * form is behind a disclosure of its own. See EntryCard.astro and
 * ProposalForm.astro, which carry the same rule.
 *
 * GATED BY THE '/profile' PREFIX IN src/lib/entitlement.ts, a policy entry
 * of its own now rather than inherited from '/account' by string match, so
 * this page reads Astro.locals.verdict the same way every other gated page
 * does.
 *
 * THE RECORD IS RENDERED THROUGH RecordView, EDITABLE, THROUGH THE
 * ENDPOINTS THAT ALREADY EXIST. No second write path to the same data: the
 * forms below post to src/pages/profile/entry.ts, .../artifact.ts and
 * .../import.ts, the only three endpoints that ever touch a record row.
 *
 * EDITING IN PLACE, INCLUDING ON SAVE. `profilePagePath` below is this
 * page's OWN address, so the per-entry "Edit" and "Cancel" links open and
 * close the edit form without leaving this page, and `returnKey="profile"`
 * tells entry.ts and artifact.ts to send the reader back here afterwards as
 * well. There is now exactly one value that key can carry, because there is
 * exactly one page left that carries these forms; see RecordView's own
 * Props for why the type still names it as a key rather than inlining the
 * one path it resolves to.
 *
 * THE COOKIE-PATH TRAP, AND WHY EVERY RELAY PATH HERE IS withBase('/profile').
 * A validation failure cannot return in a redirect's body, so entry.ts and
 * artifact.ts relay it through a short-lived, httpOnly cookie scoped, by path,
 * to whichever page posted (see RETURN_PATHS in profile/entry.ts). That scope
 * has to equal the address this page is actually read at, or the cookie a
 * failed submission set is never sent back on the reload that follows. THE
 * BROWSER COMPARES A COOKIE'S Path AGAINST THE FULL REQUEST PATH, INCLUDING THE
 * SITE BASE: this page is served at /jobs/profile, so a cookie scoped to the
 * base-free /profile is never sent, and for a long time that silently swallowed
 * every validation error. An earlier version of this comment claimed the base
 * was excluded from the comparison; it is not. Every relay path here, and the
 * matching set in entry.ts/artifact.ts/import.ts/link.ts, is withBase('/profile')
 * so the set path and the request path agree.
 *
 * WORKS WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT, AND THAT IS WHY EVERY DISCLOSURE IS <details>.
 * Every form on this page, and on RecordView and EntryCard beneath it, is a
 * plain POST to a real endpoint. The record rows, the add-entry form, the
 * paste fallback, the per-proposal review fields and the delete confirmations
 * are all native <details>, so they open and close with no script running.
 * The record's kind filter is a set of plain links read from `?kind=`, and
 * "Edit" is a plain link that sets `?edit=`. The one script on this page is
 * the upload enhancement at the foot, and everything it does has a plain
 * navigation behind it. The "Your surfaces" nav at the foot of the allowed
 * branch is the same discipline applied to navigation.
 *
 * THE IMMUTABLE CORE IS NOT VISUALLY SPECIAL HERE, ON PURPOSE. record.ts's
 * IMMUTABLE_CORE_FIELDS (employer, title, dates) are immutable to a RENDER
 * of this record, never to the person editing their own record: nothing on
 * this page locks those fields, marks them with a warning icon, or treats
 * editing them as more dangerous than any other field.
 *
 * CLASSIFICATION IS RECORDED, NOT LIVE. RUN-MASTER amendment 6 locks
 * anything above 'private' dark this run: the control exists on every
 * entry and genuinely writes what a person chooses, and the page says so
 * plainly, once, rather than hiding the control or pretending the choice
 * already does something.
 *
 * NAME, EMAIL AND HANDLE ARE READ HERE, NEVER EDITED HERE. The Identity
 * panel below is text: whoever wants to change any of the three now goes to
 * Settings, which is the one place that writes them.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../site.config.mjs';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import ImportBand from '../components/profile/ImportBand.astro';
import { isPaidViewer } from '../lib/ledger-access';
import RecordView from '../components/profile/RecordView.astro';
import { KIND_LABELS, CLASSIFICATION_LABELS, MONTH_NAMES, issueMessage } from '../components/profile/entry-presentation';
import {
  RELAY_COOKIE,
  addFormState,
  artifactFormState,
  editFormState,
  parseRelay
} from '../components/profile/record-relay';
import { routeFor } from '../data/nav';
import { MEMBER_NAV } from '../data/member-nav';
import { CEILINGS, CLASSIFICATIONS, ENTRY_KINDS } from '../lib/record';
import { getCoverLetter, listEntries, listLinks, personName } from '../lib/record-store';
import { linkPlatformLabel } from '../lib/profile-links';
import PlatformIcon from '../components/profile/PlatformIcon.astro';
import { getParse } from '../lib/resume-parse-store';
import { landReadyParse } from '../lib/resume-parse-apply';
import { keyStorageIsConfigured } from '../lib/keychain';
import { keyMeta } from '../lib/keychain-store';
import { GENERATION_PROVIDER_ORDER, PROVIDER_REGISTRY } from '../lib/generation-providers';
import { isOn } from '../lib/flags';
import { getAuth } from '../lib/auth';

export const prerender = false;

const verdict = Astro.locals.verdict;
const allowed = verdict?.allow === true;
const reason = verdict?.reason ?? 'signed-out';
const viewer = Astro.locals.viewer;
/* Reading a resume runs on the member's own key and fills the Profile Record,
   and the tiers matrix marks both paid-only, so the import band is offered to
   a paid reader alone. */
const paidViewer = isPaidViewer(viewer);

// A finished read that has not landed in the record yet lands here, before the
// name, entries and links below are read, so the rows it creates are the rows
// this page shows. Normally the background runner has already done this and
// nothing is waiting (resume-parse-apply.ts).
const landed = allowed && viewer ? await landReadyParse(viewer.userId) : null;

const name = allowed && viewer ? await personName(viewer.userId) : null;
// The account email has no reader inside src/lib/entitlement.ts's Viewer
// type (it deliberately carries only userId, tier and emailVerified), so
// this page calls src/lib/auth.ts's own getAuth().api.getSession()
// directly, the identical call viewer.ts already makes internally, to read
// session.user.email. A second session lookup per request rather than a
// shared one; tailor.astro's own header already describes making the same
// call for the same reason.
const session = allowed ? await getAuth().api.getSession({ headers: Astro.request.headers }) : null;
const email = session?.user?.email ?? null;

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The relay cookie: what a failed entry or artifact submission carried
   back. Read once, then deleted, so a reload never repeats it. See this
   file's own header on why RELAY_COOKIE_PATH is the literal '/profile'.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
const RELAY_COOKIE_PATH = withBase('/profile');
const relay = parseRelay(Astro.cookies.get(RELAY_COOKIE)?.value);
Astro.cookies.delete(RELAY_COOKIE, { path: RELAY_COOKIE_PATH });

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The import boost (MASTER-SPEC F2's parenthesis): upload a resume, which
   profile/import/parse.ts reads in the background, then review and confirm the
   proposals here. The band below is a state machine with four states, and
   exactly one is ever on screen:

   - done:    a confirm just landed. A one-line receipt, relayed the ordinary
              way through a short-lived httpOnly cookie set by import.ts, read
              once here and deleted, never the entries themselves.
   - review:  a finished read is waiting to be acted on. This is the state that
              matters most: a person who uploaded and navigated away comes back
              to their proposals, not to an empty upload box. The parse row is
              the proof it is still waiting, because import.ts clears that row
              on confirm.
   - reading: a read is still running.
   - idle:    nothing in flight. The upload band.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

interface ImportRelay {
  scope: 'import';
  created: number;
  failed: number;
  links: number;
  name: boolean;
  /** The prfIds the confirm actually created, so the record below can mark
      exactly those rows. Optional in the guard: a cookie written by the
      previous deploy has no such field, and an old receipt is worth showing
      without its marks rather than dropping on the floor. */
  createdIds: string[];
}

function parseImportRelay(raw: string | undefined): ImportRelay | null {
  if (!raw) return null;
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw) as Partial<ImportRelay>;
    if (
      parsed.scope === 'import' &&
      typeof parsed.created === 'number' &&
      typeof parsed.failed === 'number' &&
      typeof parsed.links === 'number' &&
      typeof parsed.name === 'boolean'
    ) {
      const createdIds = Array.isArray(parsed.createdIds)
        ? parsed.createdIds.filter((id): id is string => typeof id === 'string')
        : [];
      return { ...(parsed as ImportRelay), createdIds };
    }
    return null;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

const IMPORT_RELAY_COOKIE_PATH = withBase('/profile');
const importRelay = parseImportRelay(Astro.cookies.get('record_import_relay')?.value);
Astro.cookies.delete('record_import_relay', { path: IMPORT_RELAY_COOKIE_PATH });

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The links relay cookie: what a rejected add carried back (see
   profile/link.ts). Unlike the keys relay on Settings, this one may carry the
   typed value, because a link is a public URL the person needs to see to fix,
   not a secret. Read once, then deleted, so a reload never repeats it.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

interface LinkRelay {
  scope: 'link';
  url: string;
  reason: string;
}

function parseLinkRelay(raw: string | undefined): LinkRelay | null {
  if (!raw) return null;
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw) as Partial<LinkRelay>;
    if (parsed.scope === 'link' && typeof parsed.url === 'string' && typeof parsed.reason === 'string') {
      return { scope: 'link', url: parsed.url, reason: parsed.reason };
    }
    return null;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

const LINK_RELAY_COOKIE_PATH = withBase('/profile');
const linkRelay = parseLinkRelay(Astro.cookies.get('profile_link_relay')?.value);
Astro.cookies.delete('profile_link_relay', { path: LINK_RELAY_COOKIE_PATH });

// A read still running, if any. A finished read never waits here: it landed
// above, so the only parse state this page can show is 'reading'.
const parse = allowed && viewer ? await getParse(viewer.userId) : null;
const importStatusAction = routeFor('profile-import-status');

// The receipt for the band and the record's new-row marks: what landed on
// this request, else what the confirm relay cookie carried.
const receipt: ImportRelay | null = landed
  ? {
      scope: 'import',
      created: landed.created,
      failed: landed.failed,
      links: landed.links,
      name: landed.name,
      createdIds: [...landed.createdIds]
    }
  : importRelay;

/** Which of the three import states is on screen. Exactly one, always. */
type BandState = 'idle' | 'reading' | 'done';
const bandState: BandState = parse?.status === 'pending' ? 'reading' : receipt ? 'done' : 'idle';

// Whether this person can have their resume read at all: a bring-your-own-key
// application reads a resume only with the person's OWN provider key. No key,
// no read. The deterministic reader matches one strict shape and misses
// anything written differently, so it is not offered as the way in; the
// person connects a key and their own model does it. Same gate drafting uses
// (keyStorageIsConfigured, byok flag, at least one key on file).
const keyRows = allowed && viewer && keyStorageIsConfigured() && isOn('byok') ? await keyMeta(viewer.userId) : [];
const hasProviderKey = keyRows.length > 0;

// Which key the read will actually be spent on, resolved the same way
// resume-parse-runner.ts resolves it: first match in the fixed provider order.
// Named on the waiting log, because "sent to your model" is vaguer than this
// page can afford to be about somebody's own key.
const readProviderRow = GENERATION_PROVIDER_ORDER.map((id) => keyRows.find((row) => row.provider === id)).find(
  (row) => row !== undefined
);
const readProviderLabel = readProviderRow ? PROVIDER_REGISTRY[readProviderRow.provider].label : null;

const settingsPath = `${routeFor('settings')}#keys`;

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Display formatting: KIND_LABELS, CLASSIFICATION_LABELS and MONTH_NAMES are
   imported above from entry-presentation.ts, the one place that names an
   entry now. EntryCard.astro reads the same three maps to draw one entry;
   this page needs them again for its own add-an-entry form, which is not
   EntryCard's concern.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

const entries = allowed && viewer ? await listEntries(viewer.userId) : [];
const links = allowed && viewer ? await listLinks(viewer.userId) : [];

/* The record's kind filter. Plain links setting `?kind=`, filtered here, so
   it works with no script. A tab exists only for a kind that has entries:
   this record holds six kinds, not the two a resume usually fills, and a tab
   for a kind nobody has is a control that can only disappoint. */
const kindParam = Astro.url.searchParams.get('kind');
const activeKind = ENTRY_KINDS.find((kind) => kind === kindParam) ?? null;
const kindCounts = ENTRY_KINDS.map((kind) => ({
  kind,
  count: entries.filter((entry) => entry.kind === kind).length
})).filter((row) => row.count > 0);
const visibleEntries = activeKind ? entries.filter((entry) => entry.kind === activeKind) : entries;

const editParam = Astro.url.searchParams.get('edit');
const addState = addFormState(relay);
/* The add-entry form opens when the record is empty (there is nothing else to
   do on the page), or when a submission bounced and its reason is inside it. */
const addOpen = entries.length === 0 || addState.issues.length > 0;

/* This page's own address, in the one form markup needs (base included).
   See this file's header on why the relay cookie paths above stay
   base-free while this one does not. */
const profilePagePath = routeFor('profile');
const entryAction = routeFor('profile-entry');
const artifactActionPath = routeFor('profile-artifact');
const parseAction = routeFor('profile-import-parse');
const coverAction = routeFor('profile-import-cover');
const reviewPath = routeFor('profile-review');

// The cover letter on file, and its "added" date formatted for the on-file
// line. Formatting lives here (the component prints the label as given), using
// the same month names the rest of this page uses.
const coverLetterRecord = allowed && viewer ? await getCoverLetter(viewer.userId) : null;
const coverLetterOnFile = coverLetterRecord
  ? {
      sourceName: coverLetterRecord.sourceName,
      addedLabel: coverLetterRecord.addedAt
        ? (() => {
            const when = new Date(coverLetterRecord.addedAt);
            return `${MONTH_NAMES[when.getUTCMonth()]} ${when.getUTCDate()}, ${when.getUTCFullYear()}`;
          })()
        : null
    }
  : null;
const linkAction = routeFor('profile-link');

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Your profile"
  description="Your name, your email, and the Profile Record you have built."
  noindex
>
  <section class="profile-page">
    <div class="shell profile-shell">
      {
        allowed ? (
          <>
            <header class="profile-header">
              <div class="profile-header-main">
                <span class="kicker">Account</span>
                <h1>Your profile</h1>
                <p class="muted">
                  One place for your professional facts. Fill it once, and everything you generate later pulls
                  from here.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-header-stats">
                <span class="profile-stat">
                  <strong>{entries.length}</strong> {entries.length === 1 ? 'entry' : 'entries'},{' '}
                  <strong>{links.length}</strong> {links.length === 1 ? 'link' : 'links'}
                </span>
                <span class="profile-stat-private">Private, only you can see it</span>
              </div>
            </header>

            {/* ---------------------------------------------------------------
                The import band, paid only (owner, 2026-09-21). Reading a
                resume runs on the member's own key, and both the key and the
                record it fills are paid: the tiers matrix marks "Bring your
                own key" and "The Profile Record" N, N, Y. Offering the band to
                a member who is not paying was offering a way into a feature
                they do not have.

                One state at a time. Its review state lives in the slot below
                the band rather than inside it, because the script replaces
                that slot's contents wholesale with freshly rendered HTML from
                this same page.
                --------------------------------------------------------------- */}
            {paidViewer && (
              <>
            <ImportBand
              state={bandState}
              receipt={receipt}
              hasProviderKey={hasProviderKey}
              providerLabel={readProviderLabel}
              parseAction={parseAction}
              reviewPath={reviewPath}
              profilePath={profilePagePath}
              settingsPath={settingsPath}
              coverAction={coverAction}
              coverLetterOnFile={coverLetterOnFile}
            />

            {/* The script's status carrier. A finished read lands in the record
                on its own (resume-parse-apply.ts), so there is no review to
                render here: when the poll sees the read is ready, the script
                reloads the page and the new rows appear in the record below
                with a receipt in the band above. */}
            <div data-import-review-slot data-status-url={importStatusAction}></div>
              </>
            )}

            <div class="profile-two-up">
              <Panel title="Identity" class="profile-panel">
                <p class="profile-name">
                  {name && (name.firstName || name.lastName) ? `${name.firstName} ${name.lastName}`.trim() : 'No name on file'}
                </p>
                <p class="profile-email">{email ?? 'No email on file'}</p>
                <div class="profile-actions">
                  <a class="profile-link" href={routeFor('settings')}>Edit in Settings</a>
                </div>
              </Panel>

              <Panel title="Links" class="profile-panel">
                <span slot="aside" class="panel-aside">Top of every resumé and cover letter you draft</span>
                <div id="links" class="links-anchor" />

                {linkRelay && (
                  <p class="field-issue" role="alert">That link was not added: {linkRelay.reason}.</p>
                )}

                {links.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="links-list">
                    {links.map((link) => (
                      <li class="links-row">
                        <span class="links-where">
                          <PlatformIcon platform={link.platform} class="links-logo" />
                          <span>{linkPlatformLabel(link.platform)}</span>
                        </span>
                        <a class="links-url" href={link.url} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">{link.url}</a>
                        <form class="links-remove-form" method="POST" action={linkAction}>
                          <input type="hidden" name="intent" value="remove" />
                          <input type="hidden" name="linkId" value={link.id} />
                          <button class="links-remove" type="submit" aria-label={`Remove ${link.url}`}>
                            &#215;
                          </button>
                        </form>
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}

                <form class="links-add" method="POST" action={linkAction}>
                  <input type="hidden" name="intent" value="add" />
                  <label class="visually-hidden" for="link-url">Link</label>
                  <input
                    class="field-input links-add-input"
                    id="link-url"
                    type="url"
                    name="url"
                    inputmode="url"
                    autocomplete="off"
                    placeholder="Paste any link. We read what it is from the address."
                    value={linkRelay?.url ?? ''}
                  />
                  <button class="field-submit-quiet" type="submit">Add</button>
                </form>
              </Panel>
            </div>

            {/* ---------------------------------------------------------------
                The record. One band, one row per entry, everything else behind
                a disclosure.
                --------------------------------------------------------------- */}
            <section class="record-section" aria-label="Record">
              <div class="record-band">
                <span class="mono-label record-band-title">
                  Record, {entries.length} {entries.length === 1 ? 'entry' : 'entries'}
                </span>
                {kindCounts.length > 1 && (
                  <nav class="record-filters" aria-label="Filter the record by kind">
                    <a
                      class:list={['record-filter', !activeKind && 'record-filter-on']}
                      href={profilePagePath}
                      aria-current={!activeKind ? 'true' : undefined}
                    >
                      All <span class="record-filter-count">{entries.length}</span>
                    </a>
                    {kindCounts.map((row) => (
                      <a
                        class:list={['record-filter', activeKind === row.kind && 'record-filter-on']}
                        href={`${profilePagePath}?kind=${row.kind}`}
                        aria-current={activeKind === row.kind ? 'true' : undefined}
                      >
                        {KIND_LABELS[row.kind]} <span class="record-filter-count">{row.count}</span>
                      </a>
                    ))}
                  </nav>
                )}
              </div>

              <p class="record-note">
                Employer, official title and dates appear exactly as typed in everything generated from this
                record. Type them as the employer would recognize them.
              </p>

              <details class="add-entry-details" open={addOpen}>
                <summary class="add-entry-summary">Add an entry by hand</summary>
                <div class="add-entry-body">
                  {entries.length === 0 && (
                    <p class="record-note-line">
                      Nothing is here yet. Add the first entry: a role you held, a degree, a project, a
                      skill in your own words, a standalone piece of work, or a piece of recognition. Each one
                      takes under a minute.
                    </p>
                  )}
                  <form class="record-form" method="POST" action={entryAction}>
                    <input type="hidden" name="return" value="profile" />
                    <input type="hidden" name="intent" value="create" />

                    <div class="field">
                      <label class="field-label" for="add-kind">Kind</label>
                      <select class="field-input" id="add-kind" name="kind" required>
                        <option value="" disabled selected={addState.values.kind === ''}>
                          Choose a kind
                        </option>
                        {ENTRY_KINDS.map((kind) => (
                          <option value={kind} selected={addState.values.kind === kind}>
                            {KIND_LABELS[kind]}
                          </option>
                        ))}
                      </select>
                      {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'kind') && (
                        <p class="field-issue" id="add-kind-issue">{issueMessage(addState.issues, 'kind')}</p>
                      )}
                    </div>

                    <div class="field">
                      <label class="field-label" for="add-employer">Employer or institution</label>
                      <input
                        class="field-input"
                        id="add-employer"
                        type="text"
                        name="employerOrInstitution"
                        maxlength={CEILINGS.employerOrInstitution}
                        value={addState.values.employerOrInstitution}
                        aria-describedby={issueMessage(addState.issues, 'employerOrInstitution') ? 'add-employer-issue' : undefined}
                      />
                      <p class="field-hint">Required for a role held or education. Leave blank otherwise.</p>
                      {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'employerOrInstitution') && (
                        <p class="field-issue" id="add-employer-issue">{issueMessage(addState.issues, 'employerOrInstitution')}</p>
                      )}
                    </div>

                    <div class="field">
                      <label class="field-label" for="add-title">Official title</label>
                      <input
                        class="field-input"
                        id="add-title"
                        type="text"
                        name="officialTitle"
                        required
                        maxlength={CEILINGS.officialTitle}
                        value={addState.values.officialTitle}
                      />
                      {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'officialTitle') && (
                        <p class="field-issue">{issueMessage(addState.issues, 'officialTitle')}</p>
                      )}
                    </div>

                    <div class="field-row">
                      <div class="field">
                        <label class="field-label" for="add-start-year">Start year</label>
                        <input
                          class="field-input field-input-narrow"
                          id="add-start-year"
                          type="number"
                          name="startYear"
                          min="1900"
                          max="2100"
                          value={addState.values.startYear}
                        />
                      </div>
                      <div class="field">
                        <label class="field-label" for="add-start-month">Start month</label>
                        <select class="field-input field-input-narrow" id="add-start-month" name="startMonth">
                          <option value="" selected={addState.values.startMonth === ''}>Unknown</option>
                          {MONTH_NAMES.map((monthName, index) => (
                            <option value={index + 1} selected={addState.values.startMonth === String(index + 1)}>
                              {monthName}
                            </option>
                          ))}
                        </select>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="field-hint">Required for a role held, education, or a project. A skill, an artifact, or a piece of recognition can leave it blank.</p>
                    {(issueMessage(addState.issues, 'start') || issueMessage(addState.issues, 'start.year') || issueMessage(addState.issues, 'start.month')) && (
                      <p class="field-issue">
                        {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'start') ?? issueMessage(addState.issues, 'start.year') ?? issueMessage(addState.issues, 'start.month')}
                      </p>
                    )}

                    <div class="field field-checkbox">
                      <input
                        class="field-check"
                        id="add-still-here"
                        type="checkbox"
                        name="stillHere"
                        checked={addState.values.stillHere}
                      />
                      <label class="field-label field-label-inline" for="add-still-here">Still there</label>
                    </div>

                    <div class="field-row">
                      <div class="field">
                        <label class="field-label" for="add-end-year">End year</label>
                        <input
                          class="field-input field-input-narrow"
                          id="add-end-year"
                          type="number"
                          name="endYear"
                          min="1900"
                          max="2100"
                          value={addState.values.endYear}
                        />
                      </div>
                      <div class="field">
                        <label class="field-label" for="add-end-month">End month</label>
                        <select class="field-input field-input-narrow" id="add-end-month" name="endMonth">
                          <option value="" selected={addState.values.endMonth === ''}>Unknown</option>
                          {MONTH_NAMES.map((monthName, index) => (
                            <option value={index + 1} selected={addState.values.endMonth === String(index + 1)}>
                              {monthName}
                            </option>
                          ))}
                        </select>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="field-hint">Leave both blank, and leave "Still there" unchecked, only if the end date is unknown rather than absent.</p>
                    {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'end') && <p class="field-issue">{issueMessage(addState.issues, 'end')}</p>}

                    <div class="field">
                      <label class="field-label" for="add-location">Location</label>
                      <input class="field-input" id="add-location" type="text" name="location" maxlength={CEILINGS.location} value={addState.values.location} />
                    </div>

                    <div class="field">
                      <label class="field-label" for="add-description">Description</label>
                      <textarea class="field-input field-textarea" id="add-description" name="description" maxlength={CEILINGS.description} rows="4">{addState.values.description}</textarea>
                      {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'description') && <p class="field-issue">{issueMessage(addState.issues, 'description')}</p>}
                    </div>

                    <fieldset class="field-fieldset">
                      <legend class="field-legend">Classification</legend>
                      {CLASSIFICATIONS.map((value) => (
                        <div class="field-radio">
                          <input
                            class="field-check"
                            type="radio"
                            id={`add-classification-${value}`}
                            name="classification"
                            value={value}
                            checked={addState.values.classification === value}
                          />
                          <label class="field-label field-label-inline" for={`add-classification-${value}`}>
                            {CLASSIFICATION_LABELS[value]}
                          </label>
                        </div>
                      ))}
                    </fieldset>
                    {issueMessage(addState.issues, 'classification') && <p class="field-issue">{issueMessage(addState.issues, 'classification')}</p>}

                    <button class="field-submit" type="submit">Add entry</button>
                  </form>
                </div>
              </details>

              {/* editFormState and artifactFormState are bound to this page's
                  own relay here, not passed bare: both take the relay as a
                  first argument, and passing them straight through would leave
                  RecordView calling a two-argument function with one. */}
              <RecordView
                entries={visibleEntries}
                editable={true}
                editParam={editParam}
                newIds={receipt?.createdIds ?? []}
                editFormState={(entry) => editFormState(relay, entry)}
                artifactFormState={(entry) => artifactFormState(relay, entry)}
                returnKey="profile"
                recordPagePath={profilePagePath}
                entryAction={entryAction}
                artifactActionPath={artifactActionPath}
              />
            </section>

            <p class="profile-visibility-note">
              This profile is private. Public profiles are not live yet, for anyone. What you build is real and
              saved. Who can ever see it is a later decision, not this one.
            </p>

            <nav class="profile-surfaces" aria-label="Your surfaces">
              <ul class="profile-surfaces-list">
                {MEMBER_NAV.map((item) => (
                  <li>
                    {item.built ? (
                      <a class="profile-surfaces-link" href={item.href}>{item.label}</a>
                    ) : (
                      <span class="profile-surfaces-text">{item.label}</span>
                    )}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </nav>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <span class="kicker">Account</span>
            <h1>Not available</h1>
            {reason === 'email-unverified' ? (
              <>
                <p class="muted">Confirm your email and this page opens.</p>
                <div class="account-links">
                  <a class="account-link" href={routeFor('verify-email')}>Resend the link</a>
                </div>
              </>
            ) : (
              <>
                <p class="muted">Sign in to see your profile.</p>
                <div class="account-links">
                  <a class="account-link" href={routeFor('sign-in')}>Sign in</a>
                  <a class="account-link" href={routeFor('sign-up')}>No account yet? Create one.</a>
                </div>
              </>
            )}
          </>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  /**
   * The upload band's enhancement: drop a file, and read it without leaving
   * this page.
   *
   * Without this script the band still works: the dashed box is a <label>
   * around a real file input, so clicking it opens the file picker, and a
   * plain POST 303s to /profile/review, which polls itself and shows the same
   * form. With it, the person drops a file here, the ring turns here while
   * their model reads, and the filled-in review appears here, in the slot
   * below the band.
   *
   * THE LOG NARRATES ONLY WHAT IT KNOWS. /profile/import/status answers
   * "pending" or "ready" and nothing else, so this prints the four things it
   * genuinely has: what was sent, which provider key it went to (rendered into
   * a data attribute by the server, which resolved it the same way the parse
   * runner does), how long it has been waiting, and, when the read lands, the
   * read's own notes verbatim. It never claims a stage it has not been told
   * about.
   *
   * A FINISHED READ IS A RELOAD. The read lands in the record server-side
   * (resume-parse-apply.ts), and the rows it creates, the receipt and the
   * links all sit outside the slot, so the page is reloaded whole rather
   * than patched.
   *
   * Every failure falls back to something honest: a rejected start shows the
   * note line, a poll that never turns ready stops and says so, and any
   * thrown fetch is treated as "try the plain navigation instead".
   */
  const POLL_MS = 3000;
  const POLL_LIMIT = 40; // two minutes: past the read's own 55s ceiling, with slack.

  const slot = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-import-review-slot]');
  const working = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-import-working]');
  const log = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-import-log]');
  const note = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-import-note]');
  const forms = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLFormElement>('[data-import-form]'));
  const dropzone = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-dropzone]');
  const fileInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-file-input]');
  const chips = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-file-chips]');

  const statusUrl = slot?.dataset.statusUrl ?? '';
  const providerLabel = working?.dataset.providerLabel ?? '';

  const show = (el: HTMLElement | null, on: boolean) => {
    if (el) el.hidden = !on;
  };
  const say = (text: string) => {
    if (note) {
      note.textContent = text;
      note.hidden = false;
    }
  };

  /* ---- the honest log ---------------------------------------------------- */

  /** Append one line. Returns it, so a line that updates (the wait counter)
      can be held onto rather than reprinted. */
  function logLine(text: string): HTMLElement | null {
    if (!log) return null;
    const line = document.createElement('li');
    line.textContent = text;
    log.append(line);
    return line;
  }

  function formatSize(bytes: number): string {
    return bytes >= 1024 * 1024
      ? `${(bytes / (1024 * 1024)).toFixed(1)} MB`
      : `${Math.max(1, Math.round(bytes / 1024))} KB`;
  }

  /** What this submission actually sent, named from the form itself. */
  function describeSubmission(form: HTMLFormElement): string {
    const file = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input[type="file"]')?.files?.[0];
    if (file) return `sent ${file.name}, ${formatSize(file.size)}`;
    const pasted = form.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea[name="pasted"]')?.value ?? '';
    const words = pasted.trim().split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;
    return `sent ${words} ${words === 1 ? 'word' : 'words'} of pasted text`;
  }

  const setBusy = (busy: boolean) => {
    for (const form of forms) {
      const submit = form.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('button[type="submit"]');
      if (submit) submit.disabled = busy;
    }
    show(working, busy);
  };

  /* ---- the dropzone ------------------------------------------------------ */

  if (dropzone && fileInput) {
    const paint = (on: boolean) => dropzone.classList.toggle('is-dragging', on);

    dropzone.addEventListener('dragover', (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      paint(true);
    });
    dropzone.addEventListener('dragleave', () => paint(false));
    dropzone.addEventListener('drop', (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      paint(false);
      const dropped = event.dataTransfer?.files?.[0];
      if (!dropped) return;
      // Hand the drop to the real input, so the form posts exactly what it
      // would have posted had the file been chosen through the picker.
      const carrier = new DataTransfer();
      carrier.items.add(dropped);
      fileInput.files = carrier.files;
      fileInput.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true }));
    });

    fileInput.addEventListener('change', () => {
      if (!chips) return;
      chips.replaceChildren();
      const chosen = fileInput.files?.[0];
      if (!chosen) return;
      const chip = document.createElement('span');
      chip.className = 'import-chip';
      chip.textContent = `${chosen.name}, ${formatSize(chosen.size)}`;
      chips.append(chip);
    });
  }

  /* ---- the read ---------------------------------------------------------- */

  async function readStatus(): Promise<Record<string, unknown> | null> {
    try {
      const response = await fetch(statusUrl, {
        credentials: 'same-origin',
        headers: { Accept: 'application/json' }
      });
      if (!response.ok) return null;
      return (await response.json()) as Record<string, unknown>;
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
  }

  /** The read has landed by the time this page is served again: reload it
      whole so the receipt and the record's new rows show. */
  function showLandedRead(): void {
    window.location.reload();
  }

  async function watch(startedAt: number): Promise<void> {
    const waitLine = logLine('waiting, 0s');
    for (let attempt = 0; attempt < POLL_LIMIT; attempt += 1) {
      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, POLL_MS));
      if (waitLine) {
        waitLine.textContent = `waiting, ${Math.round((Date.now() - startedAt) / 1000)}s`;
      }
      const state = await readStatus();
      if (state && state.status === 'ready') {
        // The read's own account of itself, verbatim, before the review
        // replaces the log.
        if (Array.isArray(state.notes)) {
          for (const line of state.notes) if (typeof line === 'string') logLine(line);
        }
        setBusy(false);
        showLandedRead();
        return;
      }
    }
    setBusy(false);
    say('The read is taking longer than it should. Reload this page to check on it, or try the upload again.');
  }

  if (slot && forms.length > 0) {
    for (const form of forms) {
      form.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        show(note, false);
        if (slot) slot.replaceChildren();
        if (log) log.replaceChildren();
        const startedAt = Date.now();
        logLine(describeSubmission(form));
        if (providerLabel) {
          logLine(`to your ${providerLabel} key, held in memory for this one read`);
        }
        setBusy(true);

        let body: Record<string, unknown> | null = null;
        try {
          const response = await fetch(form.action, {
            method: 'POST',
            credentials: 'same-origin',
            headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
            body: new FormData(form)
          });
          body = response.ok ? ((await response.json()) as Record<string, unknown>) : null;
          if (!response.ok) {
            // Signed out mid-session or walled: the plain navigation knows
            // where to send them, so hand the submit back to the browser.
            setBusy(false);
            form.submit();
            return;
          }
        } catch {
          setBusy(false);
          say('The upload could not be sent. Check your connection and try again.');
          return;
        }

        // A read that finished immediately (a bad file, an empty paste) hands
        // its message back; show it in place, no navigation, no polling.
        if (body && body.status === 'ready') {
          setBusy(false);
          if (typeof body.note === 'string') say(body.note);
          else showLandedRead();
          return;
        }

        void watch(startedAt);
      });
    }
  }
</script>

